{"title":"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems/N2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Canada</i>)\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a4252420c86e82bb43e408670a2e24e24bec4bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0ed898727bab8c22f2056727b56376a8efea7d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in (0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> be the number whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />th digit after the decimal point is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c37cbac475f3a830d293936bd7a26b2d8f902c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle (2^n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />th digit after the decimal point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />.  Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is rational then so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4e6ba8781d42ee434379ac570532e425e7b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fd9d6165fbc6d1e6e04ca30b89ad606b50c755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${ a \\in (0,1) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> and any natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77913c6aad5be4c1e251dec4db616016780cd7ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f_a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />th digit after the decimal point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526bd77b4de5c74c1a40d9bb93c66189acdebf36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a$\" width=\"9\" height=\"8\" />.  We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526bd77b4de5c74c1a40d9bb93c66189acdebf36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a$\" width=\"9\" height=\"8\" /> is rational if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77913c6aad5be4c1e251dec4db616016780cd7ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f_a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> is periodic for sufficiently large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, i.e., if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77913c6aad5be4c1e251dec4db616016780cd7ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f_a(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> is determined by the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e349c3441562c88539c4313e65436befd51648b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />, for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e349c3441562c88539c4313e65436befd51648b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5a07f2a22fcb2626031da734012c71b549782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is rational, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e349c3441562c88539c4313e65436befd51648b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> be an integer such that for sufficiently large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b3c775e6921fab88460099158977338edd58c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f_x(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> is determined by the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e349c3441562c88539c4313e65436befd51648b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2d13e5d203a0fb7ffe7ee130980dd09b4bfd93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m = 2^r \\cdot k$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />, for some odd integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de61dde472a066a5b90a2ff0be7a2f756110011b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle k$\" width=\"9\" height=\"12\" /> and some nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fca68834c90d92622ea606b0bd71f7d42531d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle r$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />.  We note that the residue of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e349c3441562c88539c4313e65436befd51648b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle m$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> is uniquely determined by the residues of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daad33c5ef1a9aa9c69c3a4b8f2081e8ea7759e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 2^r$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> and mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de61dde472a066a5b90a2ff0be7a2f756110011b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle k$\" width=\"9\" height=\"12\" />.  Then for sufficiently large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7447db63092942e0a39cfe01d3d94174a89707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle n$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0434246537eeede33461cde7cc97ebf2e49357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 2^{n + \\phi(k)} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2^r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/6777ef062e91a5c1beb81d4e69641542553672d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 2^n \\cdot 2^{\\phi(k)} \\equiv 2^{n+\\phi(m)} \\pmod{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>so\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b17364470fb5a2c0bb87da5ffe9e89b526d71a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 2^{n+\\phi(k)} \\pmod{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d889708185175b08c0267b8e1c54909f8581aa81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f_y(n) = f_x(2^n) = f_x [2^{n+\\phi(m)}] = f_y[n+\\phi(m)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"349\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4e6ba8781d42ee434379ac570532e425e7b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" /> is rational.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Halmos&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Halmos (page does not exist)\">Template:Halmos</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2006 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/viewtopic.php?p=875055#875055\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164241\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 213/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 373/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6674/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.945      1 -total\n 71.57%    6.402      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 26.98%    2.413      1 Template:Halmos\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5153:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164241 and revision id 15782. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}